# Compare numeric results with tolerance-aware assertions

## Description

A test that compares floats exactly breaks on the next machine or library release. `assert result == expected` on arrays raises `ValueError: The truth value of an array is ambiguous`, and `(result == expected).all()` is both exact (it fails on `0.1 + 0.2`) and uninformative (it prints `False`). The libraries ship assertion helpers that compare with a relative and an absolute tolerance, handle missing values in the same position, check dtypes and labels, and print the first mismatches. Use them in every test that checks arrays or frames.

